My Aerospace Engineering Journey 🚀

About Me

I am a secondary school student in Nigeria with a strong interest in aerospace engineering, aircraft design, aerodynamics, and space exploration. I created this repository to document my learning journey, engineering experiments, projects, and progress toward becoming an aerospace engineer.

My Goals

- Learn the fundamental principles of aerodynamics and flight.
- Conduct hands-on experiments and record scientific observations.
- Develop skills in Python programming and engineering design.
- Explore aircraft, drones, and aerospace technology.
- Build a portfolio of projects that demonstrates my curiosity, problem-solving skills, and growth as a young engineer.

My Projects

1. Paper Glider Flight Experiment

Objective: Investigate how wing design affects the flight performance of a paper glider.

Activities:

- Build and test paper glider prototypes.
- Change wing designs and observe their effects.
- Measure flight distance and, where possible, flight time.
- Record results, compare designs, and draw conclusions.

Status: Initial experiment and documentation.

